A||||8||triker||Shift Kits||||5||
Z||000000||triker||04-27-2000||05:55 PM||||Has anybody had any experience with shift kits for the Fiero automatic?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-28-2000||01:26 AM||||I have a "Trans-Go" shift kit in my trans. It works Very well and have not had any problems for the past 4 years.||||reg||14
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||04-28-2000||03:24 AM||||Oreif, I'd like to get a shift kit.. I understand how it shifts faster/harder, but does it do the same thing during normal driving, or just under hard acceleration?<P>I'd hate to have the thing kick hard when it shifts when I'm just driving down the street..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||sdm1964||04-29-2000||08:12 AM||||A shift kit will always shift hard, under light or hard driving conditions. The trans is suppose to slip less, hence longer tranny life.||||reg||7
Z||000004||Oreif||04-29-2000||02:41 PM||||My shift kit shifts a little harder during normal driving but not too hard. You'll feel it shift but it won't buck the car. I have seen some shift kits where every shift feels like someone hit the car but mine isn't like that. Under full throttle it hits real hard from first to second and a little less from second to third. I can actually get a very very slight "chirp" out of the tires shifting into second at Wide open throttle.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||04-29-2000||05:33 PM||||In my mom's ford taurus, it shifts hard all the time anyway!<P>if I'm driving slowly, and let off the gas.. then touch the pedal again, the transmission kicks.. I think it's kinda cool. heh.. so I wouldn't mind if a shift kit did the same thing.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||04-29-2000||06:14 PM||||I've also learned that having very little tranny fluid can make you shift very hard!  And also at the wrong times....||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||04-30-2000||10:29 PM||||First thing with a shift kit is making sure the tranny is good in the first place.<P>I'm not sure I'd fool around to much with 84 or 85 TH125. I'm looking at about 300 pages of things GM fixed or upgraded in these trannys. Most of the upgrades got done by late 86, but even later on they kept changing things. The early ones have a nasty habit of breaking the input assembly.<P>If the thing isn't shifting right to start with there are a bunch of things that can cause it. Most of you know to check the TV cable, but there is also an internal governer in the tranny. If that gets crap in it then you can have batty shifting or even no upshifts at all.||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||04-30-2000||10:37 PM||||Hey, nothing wrong with batty shifting! Ogre, you've said in the past that the TV cable adjustment is important on the TH125 trannies. I thought my shifts were to soft, so I adjusted it so it's much firmer, but I don't know the proper way to adjust it or whether I went too far. Please enlightenment me. Oreif, I bought one of those trans-go kits, but haven't installed it yet, glad to hear you like it and it's lasted.||||reg||1
